# Test data for Island Hop, set up through its API in one line of a test.
# Everything made here is removed again when the test ends, even when the test failed
# ("at the end, call DELETE …"), so no test leaves data behind and no clean-up state is needed.
# Names carry {unique}, so a run never trips over data from another run.

Phrase: a test ferry "<name>" with <seats> seats
  As operator:
    call POST /api/v1/ferries with {"name": "<name>", "capacity": <seats>}
    backend should reply 201 Created
    remember data.id as ferry
    at the end, call DELETE /api/v1/ferries/{ferry}


Phrase: a test port "<name>"
  As admin:
    call POST /api/v1/ports with {"name": "<name>", "timeZone": "America/Anguilla"}
    backend should reply 201 Created
    remember data.id as port
    at the end, call DELETE /api/v1/ports/{port}


# Open for trips. It borrows the photo of an existing route (the API wants one).
Phrase: a test route from "<from>" to "<to>"
  As admin:
    call GET /api/v1/ports?limit=100
    remember data.data[name="<from>"].id as from port
    remember data.data[name="<to>"].id as to port
    call GET /api/v1/routes?limit=1
    remember data.routes[0].imageUrl as route photo
    call POST /api/v1/routes with {"departurePortId": {from port}, "destinationPortId": {to port}, "durationMinutes": 60, "description": "HumanTest route {unique}", "imageUrl": {route photo}}
    backend should reply 201 Created
    remember data.id as route
    at the end, call DELETE /api/v1/routes/{route}


# Test trips leave far ahead (300 days or more) with an adult fare of $77, so no traveller books one by chance.
# The times are Anguilla time, like the operator's form.
# Don't use this one in a test: it doesn't undo itself. Use one of the two below.
Phrase: a new trip on "<ferry>" from "<from>" to "<to>", <leaves> to <arrives>, in <days> days
  As operator:
    call GET /api/v1/ferries?limit=100
    remember data.items[name="<ferry>"].id as trip ferry
    call GET /api/v1/routes?limit=100
    remember data.routes[departurePort.name="<from>", destinationPort.name="<to>"].id as trip route
    call POST /api/v1/operator/schedules with {"routeId": {trip route}, "ferryId": {trip ferry}, "departureTime": "{in <days> days}T<leaves>", "arrivalTime": "{in <days> days}T<arrives>", "adultFare": 77}
    backend should reply 201 Created
    remember data.id as trip


# Deleted when the test ends.
Phrase: a test trip on "<ferry>" from "<from>" to "<to>", <leaves> to <arrives>, in <days> days
  a new trip on "<ferry>" from "<from>" to "<to>", <leaves> to <arrives>, in <days> days
  As operator:
    at the end, call DELETE /api/v1/operator/schedules/{trip}


# For a test that books it: Island Hop never deletes a trip that has (or had) a booking, even a
# cancelled one ("Please cancel the trip instead"), so this trip is cancelled when the test ends.
# A cancelled trip doesn't block its ferry, so the next run can schedule the same time again.
Phrase: a test trip to book on "<ferry>" from "<from>" to "<to>", <leaves> to <arrives>, in <days> days
  a new trip on "<ferry>" from "<from>" to "<to>", <leaves> to <arrives>, in <days> days
  As operator:
    at the end, call PATCH /api/v1/operator/schedules/{trip}/status with {"status": "CANCELLED"}
